\p
\v 7 They donated cash¦218191 to¦218192 the stone-workers¦218192 and¦218193 carpenters¦218193, and¦218194 food¦218194, drink¦218195, and¦218196 oil¦218196 to¦218197 the workers from Tsidon \add !(Sidon)\add* and¦218198 Tsor \add !(Tyre)\add* to \add ≈float\add* cedar¦218201 \add logs along the coast\add* from¦218202 Lebananon into¦218205 Port¦218208 Yafo¦218208 \add !(Joppa¦218208)\add* with the¦218209 permission¦218209 of¦218209 Persian King¦218211 Koresh¦218210 \add !(Cyrus)\add*.
\rem /s1 Foundation Laid for the Temple
\p
\v 8 In¦218217 the¦218218 second month¦218225 of¦218219 second year¦218217 \add ≈since their¦218219 return to\add* Yerushalem¦218224, Shealtiel's¦218231 son Zerubavel¦218228 and Yotsadak's¦218235 son Yeshua¦218232, and¦218236 the¦218236 rest¦218236 of¦218236 their¦218237 brothers¦218237 the¦218239 priests¦218239 and¦218240 the¦218240 Levites¦218240, and¦218241 \add ≈everyone¦218241 except who'd¦218243 returned¦218243\add* to Yerushalem from¦218244 captivity¦218244, began¦218227 work on God's residence, and¦218246 they¦218246 appointed¦218246 the¦218249 Levites¦218249 who were twenty¦218251 and¦218253 over¦218255 to¦218254 act¦218254 as¦218254 overseers¦218254 for the¦218257 work¦218257 of¦218257 \add rebuilding\add* Yahweh's¦218260 \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 9 \add ≈And¦218263\add* Yeshua¦218264 with his¦218265 brothers and their sons, Kadmiel¦218267 and¦218268 his¦218268 sons¦218269, (all descendants of¦218269 Yehudah¦218271) \add ≈cooperated\add* to¦218273 act¦218273 as¦218273 overseers¦218273 for those doing the¦218277 work¦218277 at the \add ≈temple¦218278\add* \add together with\add* Henadad's¦218282 sons¦218283 \add ≈and grandsons\add*, and their brothers the¦218285 Levites¦218285.
\p
\v 10 \add ≈When¦218287 the¦218288 builders¦218288 had\add* laid the¦218291 \add ≈foundation¦218287\add* of¦218291 Yahweh's¦218292 temple¦218291, they¦218293 \add ≈got\add* the¦218294 priests¦218294 \add ≈to stand there in their robes\add* with¦218296 \add &their\add* trumpets¦218296, and¦218297 Asaf's¦218300 descendants¦218298 (who were Levites¦218297) with¦218301 \add &their\add* cymbals¦218301, to¦218302 praise¦218302 Yahweh¦218305 \add ≈using the¦218308 rhythms composed by\add* David¦218309, the¦218310 \add former\add* Israeli¦218312 king¦218310.\x + \xo 3:10: \xt 1Ch 25:1.\x*
\v 11 Then¦218314 they¦218314 sang¦218314 in response—praising¦218315 and¦218316 thanking¦218316 Yahweh¦218317: “\add ≈Yes,\add* he¦218319 is¦218319 good¦218319, because¦218320 his¦218323 loyal¦218323 commitment to Yisrael¦218326 \add ≈will continue forever¦218322\add*.”
\p Then¦218327 all¦218327 the¦218329 people¦218329 shouted¦218330 a¦218331 great¦218333 shout¦218331 in praise¦218334 to¦218335 Yahweh¦218335 because¦218336 the¦218338 \add ≈foundation¦218337\add* of¦218338 Yahweh's¦218340 \add temple\add* had been laid.\x + \xo 3:11: \xt 1Ch 16:34; 2Ch 5:13; 7:3; Psa 100:5; 106:1; 107:1; 118:1; 136:1; Jer 33:11.\x*
\v 12 Many¦218343 of¦218344 the¦218344 older¦218348 priests¦218344 and¦218345 Levites¦218345, and¦218346 \add ≈clan leaders\add* who'd¦218349 seen¦218350 the first¦218354 \add ≈temple¦218357\add*, wept¦218359 loudly \add ≈when¦218355 they witnessed\add* the¦218357 founding¦218355 of¦218358 this¦218356 \add *one\add*, \add ≈but¦218362 others were shouting¦218363 happily¦218363 with¦218364 loud voices¦218366\add*.
\v 13 \add ≈So¦218368\add* the¦218369 people¦218369 couldn't differentiate the¦218371 happy sounds¦218371 from the sound¦218374 of¦218375 the¦218375 people weeping¦218375, because¦218377 the¦218378 people¦218378 were¦218379 shouting¦218379 \add ≈very loudly and¦218382 it¦218383 could be¦218383 heard¦218383 from¦218386 far away\add*.
\c 4
