\v 5 \add ≈However, God¦218974 was¦218975 watching over the¦218978 Jewish leaders¦218978\add*, and¦218980 they¦218982 weren't \add actually\add* stopped¦218982. \add ≈A report¦218986 was sent¦218990\add* to¦218987 \add King\add* Dareyavesh¦218987, \add ≈then¦218989 they waited for a response\add*.
\rem /s1 Tattenai's Letter to King Darius
\v 6 Tattenai¦219002, the¦219004 governor¦219004 of¦219004 \add ≈the¦219005 province¦219005 west of the¦219007 river¦219007\add*, and Shetar¦219008-Bozenai and¦219010 his¦219010 companions¦219010, the¦219011 \add ≈provincial\add* officials¦219011, sent¦219001 the¦218998 letter¦218998 to¦219015 King¦219018 Dareyavesh¦219017 \add !(Darius¦219017)\add*—
\v 7 this¦219023 is what was¦219024 written¦219024 in¦219025 their report:
\p “To¦219026 King¦219027 Dareyavesh¦219026. All¦219029 peace¦219028.
\v 8 Let¦219034 it¦219034 be¦219034 known¦219032 to¦219035 the¦219035 king¦219035 that¦219036 we¦219038 went¦219038 to¦219039 the¦219040 province¦219040 of Yehudah, to¦219041 the¦219041 \add ≈temple¦219041\add* of¦219041 the¦219043 great¦219043 God¦219042, and¦219044 it is¦219045 being¦219045 built¦219045 with large \add #stones¦219046\add*, and¦219048 timber¦219048 is¦219049 being¦219049 placed¦219049 in¦219050 the¦219050 walls¦219050. This¦219052 work¦219051 is¦219054 being¦219054 done¦219054 \add ≈to a high standard\add* and¦219055 \add ≈they're making good progress\add*.
\p
\v 9 “Then¦219059 we¦219060 asked¦219060 those¦219062 elders¦219061, ‘Who¦219068 \add ≈gave you¦219071 all permission to¦219075 rebuild¦219075 this¦219077 temple¦219073\add*?’
