\p
\v 11 “This¦219115 is the¦219097 answer they¦219098 \add ≈gave\add* us¦219098, ‘We¦219100 are¦219102 servants¦219102 of¦219103 the¦219105 god¦219105 of¦219105 the¦219106 heavens¦219106 and¦219107 earth¦219107, and¦219108 we¦219108 are¦219108 \add ≈rebuilding the¦219109 temple¦219109\add* that¦219110 was¦219112 constructed and¦219122 finished¦219122 many¦219117 years¦219116 \add ≈ago by a¦219118 famous¦219120 Israeli¦219119\add* king¦219118.
\v 12 However, because our¦219129 ancestors¦219129 made the god¦219130 of the¦219131 heavens¦219131 angry¦219128, he¦219132 let Babylonian King¦219136 Nevukadnetstsar¦219135 (\add Nebuchadnezzar,\add* the¦219139 Chaldean¦219139) \add ≈defeat them\add*, and¦219141 he¦219143 destroyed¦219143 \add ≈that¦219127 temple¦219141\add* and¦219144 caused the¦219144 people¦219144 to¦219145 be exiled¦219145 to¦219146 Babylon¦219146.\x + \xo 5:12: \xt 2Ki 25:8-12; 2Ch 36:17-20; Jer 52:12-15.\x*
\v 13 But in¦219150 the first year¦219150 \add of the reign of\add* Babylonian King Koresh \add !(Cyrus)\add*, \add *he\add* made¦219158 a¦219159 decree¦219159 to¦219164 rebuild¦219164 this¦219163 house¦219160 of¦219160 God¦219162.\x + \xo 5:13: \xt Ezr 1:2-11.\x*
\v 14 \add ≈What's more,\add* the¦219174 gold¦219174 and¦219175 silver¦219175 \add ≈containers¦219167\add* that¦219176 Nevukadnetstsar¦219177 had¦219178 taken¦219178 out¦219178 from¦219179 that temple¦219181 that¦219182 was¦219183 in¦219183 Yerushalem¦219183 and¦219184 had brought¦219184 to¦219186 the¦219186 temple¦219186 in Babylon¦219188, King¦219192 Koresh¦219191 took¦219189 them out from¦219193 the¦219195 temple¦219195 in Babylon¦219197 and¦219198 they¦219198 were¦219198 \add ≈handed¦219198 over\add* to¦219199 the man named¦219200 Sheshbatstsar who¦219201 he'd¦219203 appointed as governor¦219202 \add over Yehudah\add*.
\v 15 \add @Koresh¦219205\add* had told¦219205 him to take¦219212 those¦219209 containers¦219211 and put them¦219216 back in¦219217 the¦219217 temple¦219217 in¦219219 Yerushalem¦219219, and¦219220 \add ≈to ensure that¦219218 the¦219220 temple¦219220 got rebuilt¦219222 in the¦219221 same place¦219225 where it¦219222 had been¦219222 before\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈So\add* Sheshbatstsar came¦219231 \add here\add* and laid¦219232 the¦219233 \add #foundation¦219233\add* of¦219234 God's¦219237 house¦219236 in¦219239 Yerushalem¦219239, and¦219240 since then¦219242, it's¦219246 been¦219246 being¦219246 rebuilt¦219246 but¦219247 isn't¦219247 finished¦219248 yet.’
\p
\v 17 \add ≈So¦219250\add* now¦219250, if¦219251 it \add ≈pleases¦219255\add* the¦219254 king¦219254, let¦219256 a search¦219256 be¦219256 made¦219273 in¦219257 \add the records in\add* the¦219261 king's¦219261 treasure¦219258 house there¦219262 in¦219264 Babylon¦219264, if it's¦219255 \add correct\add* that¦219267 a¦219274 decree¦219274 was set by King Koresh¦219271 to¦219275 rebuild¦219275 this house¦219276 of¦219276 God¦219278 in¦219280 Yerushalem¦219280. Then¦219281 let the¦219282 king¦219282 send¦219286 his decision on this matter back to¦219287 us¦219287.”
\c 6
