\s1 Ezra finds some Levites to take
\rem /s1 The Return to Jerusalem; Servants for the Temple; Ezra's Journey to Jerusalem
\p
\v 15 \add Firstly,\add* I¦220479 gathered¦220479 them¦220479 \add ≈near\add* the¦220482 river¦220482 that¦220483 goes¦220483 to¦220484 Ahava¦220486, and¦220487 we¦220487 camped¦220487 there¦220488 for three¦220490 days¦220489. I¦220491 \add ≈interviewed\add* the people¦220492 and¦220493 the priests¦220493 and¦220494 \add ≈discovered¦220498 that we didn't¦220496 have any¦220494 Levites included\add* \add in the group\add*.
\v 16 \add ≈So¦220501 I¦220501 summoned\add* the following leaders¦220511: Eliezer¦220502, Ariel¦220503, Shemayah¦220504, Elnatan¦220505, Yarib¦220506, \add a second\add* Elnatan¦220507, Natan¦220508, Zekaryah¦220509, and¦220510 Meshullam¦220510, as well as the wise men: Yoyariv¦220512 and¦220513 \add a third\add* Elnatan¦220513.
\v 17 I¦220516 commanded¦220516 them¦220518 to go to¦220519 Iddo¦220521, the¦220522 leader¦220522 at Kasifya¦220523, and¦220525 I¦220525 \add ≈told them to tell\add* Iddo¦220531 and his¦220532 relatives¦220532 (temple¦220533 servants¦220533 in¦220535 Kasifya¦220535) to¦220537 send¦220537 us¦220539 \add @some Levites\add* who would \add go to Yerushalem to\add* serve in our¦220542 god's¦220542 \add ≈temple\add*.
\v 18 \add ≈Then¦220544 since we had God's¦220548 favour\add*, they sent us¦220550 a¦220551 \add ≈talented\add* man¦220551 (from¦220553 the¦220553 sons¦220553 of¦220554 Mahli¦220554, son¦220555 of¦220555 Levi¦220557, son¦220558 of¦220558 Yisrael¦220560) and eighteen of¦220562 his¦220562 sons and¦220563 \add ≈other relatives¦220563\add*.
