\v 24 Then¦220655 I¦220655 chose twelve of¦220656 the¦220656 leaders¦220656 of¦220657 the¦220657 priests¦220657 along with Sherevyah and Hashavyah¦220661 and¦220662 ten of the other Levites,
\v 25 and¦220666 \add as they watched,\add* I¦220666 weighed¦220666 out¦220666 the¦220675 gold¦220675 and silver¦220672, and the¦220678 \add valuable\add* utensils¦220678—the¦220679 offering for the¦220680 house¦220680 of¦220680 our¦220682 god¦220682 that¦220683 the¦220684 king¦220684, and¦220685 his¦220685 counsellors¦220685 and¦220686 officials¦220686, and¦220687 all¦220687 the \add ≈exiled Israelis¦220689 who¦220690 could be¦220690 contacted\add*, had offered¦220683.
\v 26 \add ≈It came to\add* three tonnes of gold¦220707, twenty-one tonnes of silver¦220696, and another three tonnes of¦220702 silver¦220704 containers¦220702,
\v 27 as well as twenty¦220713 gold bowls¦220711 that weighed another eight kilograms, and¦220716 two¦220720 polished bronze¦220717 containers¦220716 that were as valuable as gold¦220722.
\p
\v 28 “You¦220726 are¦220727 sacred¦220727 to¦220728 Yahweh¦220728,” I told¦220724 them¦220725 all, “and¦220729 the¦220729 \add ≈containers¦220729 and utensils¦220729\add* are¦220730 sacred¦220730, and¦220732 the¦220732 gold¦220732 and silver¦220731 are¦220733 a¦220733 freewill¦220733 offering¦220733 to¦220734 Yahweh¦220734, the¦220735 god¦220735 of¦220735 your¦220736 ancestors¦220736.
