\p
\v 31 Then¦220769 in mid-April, we¦220769 set¦220769 out¦220769 from¦220770 the¦220770 river¦220770 Ahava¦220771 to¦220776 go¦220776 to Yerushalem¦220777, and¦220778 \add ≈we had God's¦220780 favour as he¦220783 kept us¦220783 safe from¦220784 any enemies¦220785 or ambushes¦220786\add* on¦220787 the¦220789 way¦220789.
\v 32 \add ≈So¦220791\add* we¦220791 arrived¦220791 at Yerushalem¦220792, and¦220793 \add ≈rested¦220793\add* there¦220794 for three¦220796 days¦220795.
\v 33 On¦220798 the¦220799 fourth¦220799 day¦220798, the¦220801 gold¦220802 and silver¦220801 and¦220802 the¦220802 \add ≈containers¦220803 and¦220803 utensils¦220803\add* were weighed¦220800 out¦220800 in¦220804 the \add ≈temple¦220804\add*—\add ≈being handed¦220807 over to\add* Uriyah's¦220812 son Meremot¦220809, the¦220813 priest¦220813, and¦220814 with¦220814 him¦220814 was Pinhas's¦220818 son Eleazar¦220815 (and¦220819 with¦220819 them¦220819 were Yeshua's¦220823 son Yozavad¦220820, and Binnuy's¦220827 son Noadyah¦220824, the Levites¦220828).
\v 34 \add ≈They recorded¦220833 all¦220834 the¦220836 items with their weights¦220836\add*.
\p
